<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Chernaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1855</span> · Also known as Battle of the Tchernaya · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Chernaya was fought on 16 August 1855 on the Chernaya river near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sevastopol">Sevastopol</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a>. French and Sardinian troops beat off a Russian attack meant to relieve the besieged city, which fell three weeks later. It was the Sardinian contingent's main battle and helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camillo-benso-count-of-cavour">Cavour</a> win a place for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> at the peace congress in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-chernaya.jpg" alt="Battle of the Chernaya" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Simpson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_the_Tchernaya,_August_16th_1855.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
